# Who is asked to review what.
#
# One line, because there is one maintainer. The ruleset on `main` requires no approval
# (required_approving_review_count is 0), so the effect here is not a gate: it is the automatic
# review request on every pull request. That matters the day someone outside the project opens
# one, and costs nothing until then.
#
# Requiring the review would mean turning on require_code_owner_review in
# .github/rulesets/main.json — which, with a single owner, would lock the maintainer out of their
# own repository, since GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request.

